To help fuel the ColorRisk version, here's some more info:

The version I have is 2.41, and was completed in mid 1990.  It is in FULL
color, including backgrounds.  There was a substantially smaller
version 2.40, but it had B&W backgrounds.  I can find no names listed on
the program, so I can't tell if it's from the same guy who negotiated
with Parker Brothers, although it plays exactly the same.  I will be
checking inside the bugger soon, though, in case there's a name buried
somewhere that mortal men were never meant to see...

BTW, I can't figure out why PB would have any complaints with the computer
version.  My friends and I are so addicted to it that WE BOUGHT THE BOARD
GAME ITSELF for more fun.  If that isn't a good marketing ploy, I've been
hearing too many Phil's Gum City commercials on the radio.  Of course, if
Parker Brothers, doesn't want us to buy their games, well...

And remember - good strategy says "take Austrailia first".
